---
import LegalLayout from '../../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const alternates = { hu: '/adatkezeles/', en: '/en/privacy/' };
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy notice"
  updated="Effective: 20 September 2026"
  alternates={alternates}
>
  <p>
    This notice explains what personal data <strong>kiroland.hu</strong> processes, for what purpose,
    and what rights you have. The site is a personal portfolio: it sells nothing, requires no
    registration, and does not profile its visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>Data controller</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>Name</dt>
    <dd>{site.name}</dd>
    <dt>Email</dt>
    <dd><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></dd>
    <dt>Website</dt>
    <dd>https://kiroland.hu</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>Contact form</h2>
  <p>
    If you send a message through the form, the details arrive to me by email. Nobody else has
    access to them, and they are not stored in any database.
  </p>
  <dl>
    <dt>Data processed</dt>
    <dd>name, email address, the text of your message, the time of sending</dd>
    <dt>Purpose</dt>
    <dd>replying to your enquiry and keeping in touch</dd>
    <dt>Legal basis</dt>
    <dd>your consent (GDPR Article 6(1)(a)), given via the checkbox on the form</dd>
    <dt>Retention</dt>
    <dd>at most 2 years, or until you withdraw your consent</dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    Giving consent is voluntary, but without it I cannot accept your message. You may withdraw it at
    any time: write to the address above and I will delete your enquiry from my mailbox.
  </p>

  <h2>Spam protection — Google reCAPTCHA</h2>
  <p>
    The form is protected against automated submissions by Google reCAPTCHA v3. The service
    <strong>only starts</strong> when you begin using the form — if you are merely browsing the
    site, no data reaches Google.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once started, Google receives the data needed to operate the system, including your IP address,
    browser information and interactions on the page, and it also uses data stored on its own
    domain. Processing may take place in the United States. Details are in Google's
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>
    and <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">terms of service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site <strong>uses no cookies</strong> and stores nothing in your browser. There is no
    analytics, advertising or social media tracking. Cookies may only be set by the reCAPTCHA
    described above, and only if you use the form.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted by <strong>Nethely Kft.</strong> (Hungary). For operational and security
    reasons the provider logs requests, which may include visitors' IP addresses. I access these
    logs in line with the provider's policy and do not combine them with any other data.
  </p>

  <h2>Processors and recipients</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Nethely Kft.</strong> — hosting and email delivery</li>
    <li><strong>Google Ireland Limited</strong> — operating the reCAPTCHA service</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your data is not shared with anyone else and is never used for marketing.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>request information about the data I hold about you</li>
    <li>request the correction of inaccurate data</li>
    <li>request erasure or restriction of processing</li>
    <li>object to the processing</li>
    <li>request your data in a portable format</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A single email to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> is enough for any of these.
    I will reply within 30 days at the latest.
  </p>

  <h2>Remedies</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe your rights have been infringed, you may lodge a complaint with the Hungarian
    National Authority for Data Protection and Freedom of Information (NAIH, 1055 Budapest, Falk
    Miksa utca 9–11., <a href="https://naih.hu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">naih.hu</a>), or turn
    to the courts.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    If the way the site works changes, I will update this notice. The date of the latest change is
    shown at the top of the page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
